cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CAPE-Loop, cite the software using this metadata. Citation
  metadata for the associated paper will be added when it is available.
title: "CAPE-Loop: Causal Attribution of Preference Evidence in Closed-Loop Agents"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "CAPE-Loop contributors"
abstract: >-
  CAPE-Loop is a controlled evaluation framework for studying whether
  persistent agent profiles account for the causal provenance of user
  responses and whether profile-conditioned interaction can create
  self-confirming user models.
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - language-model agents
  - personalization
  - persistent profiles
  - user modeling
license: Apache-2.0
